   "evidence": "Multipole.lean:156-159 \u2014 `private lemma prod_ofFn_mul_mul_inv {G : Type*} [Group G] : \u2200 {k : \u2115} (a : Fin (k+1) \u2192 G) (A : Fin k \u2192 G), (List.ofFn fun i => a i.castSucc * A i * (a i.succ)\u207b\u00b9).prod = a 0 * (List.ofFn A).prod * (a (Fin.last k))\u207b\u00b9`. No upstream equivalent: Mathlib's telescoping list lemmas are `List.prod_range_div'` (Group, `f k / f (k+1)`, Mathlib/Algebra/BigOperators/Group/List/Basic.lean:332) and `List.prod_range_div` (CommGroup, line 353) \u2014 neither carries the inner factor `A i`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/SmallX/Dipole/Multipole.lean",
   "fix": "Move it to its canonical home as a public `List.prod_ofFn_mul_mul_inv` in a `List`-namespace module mirroring `Mathlib/Algebra/BigOperators/Group/List/Basic.lean` (upstream-namespace, PhyslibAlpha-eligible per CLAUDE.md), and import it in `Multipole.lean`.",
   "issue": "`private lemma prod_ofFn_mul_mul_inv` is general infrastructure, not a step specific to this argument: its statement mentions only `Group`, `List.ofFn`, `Fin.castSucc/succ/last`, and its proof is a bare induction with no reference to Wilson lines, traces, or `multipoleS`. Hiding it makes a standalone telescoping-conjugation identity unavailable to any other caller.",
   "line": "156"
  }
